> Jordan had practiced the free-throw routine so often that his sneakers knew the floorboards. Still, the gym felt different on scholarship night. Banners whispered overhead. His little sister waved from the bleachers with a poster that misspelled his name and somehow made him braver.…

Turn and talk: Which earlier habit from Unit 2 might help today?

## Teach

### Big idea

Reading is thinking with a text. Today’s skill — **Stamina Strategies for Long Text** — sits inside Reading: Key Ideas — Long Passages. We will slow down, annotate, and back every claim with evidence a classmate could find.

### Why it matters

At Prosper Prep, clear reading and writing support scholarship habits: follow directions, cite evidence, and revise until a stranger can follow your thinking. Families use these skills when reading news, contracts, team emails, and faith or community texts. East Texas students deserve elite literacy tools — not tricks.

