2. Name the common mistake to avoid today (hint: related to treating two true facts as if…).
3. Create one new practice item (with answer) a classmate could try in 2 minutes.

*(Scored exit items also appear as multiple-choice checks below the lesson in Prosper Prep.)*

## Stretch (optional)

Write a short CER paragraph (4–6 sentences) about the mentor passage that depends on “Long-Passage Key Ideas Check.” Label C / E / R in the margin. Then invent a harder follow-up question for a classmate.
