## Warm-up (3–5 minutes)

Skim this mini-passage once, then write one sentence naming what it seems to be mostly about:

> School start times are a tug-of-war between biology and logistics. Many middle-school students naturally fall asleep later, so early bells can cut into deep sleep. Sleep researchers argue that even modest delays can improve alertness and mood.…

Turn and talk: Which earlier habit from Unit 7 might help today?

## Teach

### Big idea

Reading is thinking with a text. Today’s skill — **Speech Excerpt: Purpose and Tone** — sits inside Reading: Craft — Long Passages. We will slow down, annotate, and back every claim with evidence a classmate could find.

